# A circuit with long-range two-qubit gates, used to demo verified routing.
# On a linear coupling map 0-1-2-3 the q0-q3 and q1-q3 gates are not physically
# adjacent, so `daedalus route routed_line.qf --coupling line --verify` inserts
# SWAPs and proves the result equivalent up to the final qubit layout.
qubits 4
bits 1
h q0
cx q0, q3
cz q1, q3
t q3
cx q0, q2
measure q3 -> c0
